{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lin, one of the psychiatry residents. I’m here to talk with you about what happened tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just… I threw a table. I don’t know why. I was at home and everything felt too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Can you tell me what ‘too much’ felt like? Were you upset, angry, overwhelmed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Both. Angry and scared. Like I couldn’t breathe. My chest was tight. I felt like I was disappearing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really intense. Have you felt that way before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:36:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah. A few times. Last month, I drove too fast on the highway. But I didn’t want to crash. I just wanted to feel something real."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:37:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I remember that from your last admission. You were doing ECT then, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:38:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I was. But I stopped after I got out. I thought I was okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:39:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common for symptoms to come back if treatment is interrupted, especially with bipolar and borderline personality disorder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:40:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just… I don’t want to keep doing this. Breaking things. Feeling like I’m not here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-10-03 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to help you stabilize. You’re safe here. We’ll start by adjusting your medications and getting you back into therapy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I reviewed your chart. You’re on levothyroxine for hypothyroidism—still taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I have it at home. I’ve been skipping it sometimes. I forget."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:17:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thyroid levels can affect your mood and energy. We’ll make sure you get it daily while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:18:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my endometriosis pain—it’s been worse lately. I’ve been using ibuprofen, but it’s not helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:20:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Chronic pain can make emotional regulation harder. We’ll manage it carefully—avoiding opioids since there’s a history of abuse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:21:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I shouldn’t use them. But when the pain hits, I just want it gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-10-04 09:22:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll work on non-opioid strategies and explore what triggers the flare-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-10-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve updated your meds. We’re restarting lamotrigine for bipolar and adding naltrexone to help with cravings."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-10-05 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Naltrexone? For alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-10-05 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You mentioned drinking a few times a week to cope. Naltrexone can reduce the urge and help you stay in control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-10-05 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to be dependent on anything. Not pills, not alcohol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-10-05 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This isn’t about dependence. It’s about support. Like using a cane when your leg is weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-10-05 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess… I can try it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-10-06 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling today? Any changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-10-06 14:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little calmer. Still sad sometimes. But I didn’t have that ‘disappearing’ feeling yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-10-06 14:32:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’re also going to restart ECT twice a week. It helped before—let’s see if it helps now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-10-06 14:33:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared of it. The memory loss…"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-10-06 14:35:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use the lowest effective dose. Most people notice improvement in mood without major memory issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-10-06 14:36:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. If it helps me feel real again, I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-10-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had your first ECT yesterday. How did you feel afterward?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-10-08 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired. A little confused for a few hours. But this morning, I cried when I saw a photo of my cat. I haven’t felt anything like that in weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-10-08 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign. Feeling emotions again means the numbness is lifting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-10-08 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to go back to feeling nothing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-10-08 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re building a plan to prevent that—meds, ECT, and therapy. DBT starts tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-10-09 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How was the first DBT group?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-10-09 11:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "We talked about distress tolerance. I liked the idea of ‘surfing the wave’ instead of reacting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-10-09 11:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Emotions rise and fall. You don’t have to act on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-10-09 11:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But what if I can’t stop myself? Like with the table?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-10-09 11:04:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what the skills are for. And we’ll keep your meds optimized. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-10-11 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two ECT sessions. Any side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-10-11 10:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My head hurts a little after, but Tylenol helps. And I’m remembering things—like what I ate, what we talked about."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-10-11 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. That means your cognition is stable. Your mood reports are improving too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-10-11 10:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still have days where I feel empty. But not every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-10-11 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Recovery isn’t linear. The fact that you’re noticing the difference is progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-10-13 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re halfway through your stay. Discharge planning has started. How do you feel about going home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-10-13 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared. What if I fall apart again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-10-13 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have support. Weekly ECT for now, DBT group, and your psychiatrist will see you every two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-10-13 14:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel like I’m losing it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-10-13 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You call your crisis line, go to the ER, or come back here. Your safety plan will list all the steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-10-15 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. Thyroid levels are stable. That’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-10-15 09:46:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that wasn’t making me worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-10-15 09:47:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not this time. But staying on it helps prevent mood swings. We’ll keep you on the same dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-10-15 09:48:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll try not to skip it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-10-16 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow is your last ECT session here. After discharge, it will continue outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-10-16 13:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about going off-site for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-10-16 13:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll arrange transportation. And you’ll have a contact person at the clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-10-16 13:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I don’t want to lose the progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final day. You’ve done really well. Mood more stable, engaging in therapy, no self-harm thoughts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still have hard moments. But I’m using the skills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what matters. Keep using them. Here’s your discharge packet—meds, appointments, crisis plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if I need to come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can always come back. This isn’t failure. It’s part of recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. For not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-10-17 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re a team. Take care of yourself. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-10-03 20:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-10-18 01:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman was admitted to the psychiatry service after an outburst in which she threw a table during a period of emotional dysregulation. She has a history of bipolar disorder, borderline personality disorder, chronic pain from endometriosis, and substance use involving alcohol, opioids, and sedatives. During her 15-day admission, she was restarted on lamotrigine and initiated on naltrexone to support mood stabilization and reduce cravings. Electroconvulsive therapy was resumed and administered three times weekly with improvement in mood and affect. She engaged in dialectical behavior therapy, improved adherence to levothyroxine, and developed a crisis plan. By discharge, she denied suicidal ideation, demonstrated use of coping skills, and was transitioned to outpatient ECT and intensive therapy with close follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Bipolar disorder, current episode mixed, unspecified",
      "Sedative, hypnotic or anxiolytic abuse, uncomplicated",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Opioid abuse, uncomplicated",
      "Alcohol abuse, uncomplicated",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Endometriosis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
